      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith multiple data-parallel workers, `_execute_profile` waits for all profiling replies but checks only the first one received. A successful reply followed by a failed reply therefore reports success, while the reverse arrival order raises an error. Both `start_profile` and `stop_profile` share this helper.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAggregate the replies with the existing `FanOutCommunicator.merge_results` helper and raise if any worker fails. Preserve the original first response object when all workers succeed.\n\nAdd CPU regressions using the real fan-out communicator for single-worker failure, both reply orders, a failure between successful replies, and all-success response preservation with one, two, and four workers.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The registered CPU test now initializes the repository's existing `maybe_stub_sgl_kernel()` helper before serving imports, matching neighboring CPU tests. Without this initialization, direct execution on a Mac without `sgl_kernel` failed during import before reaching any assertions. Production code and all seven test scenarios are unchanged by this follow-up.\n- Direct registered-test execution on macOS with Python 3.12: **two methods / seven scenarios pass**, using the real `CustomTestCase`, complete control module, real communicator, and actual IPC classes. The repository-provided optional-kernel/Mac compatibility layers are active; this is not GPU-kernel validation, and no external AST/module-isolation harness is used.\n- With only the production control module reverted to parent `6b33338242f8ce85cd66bac96a396a4ddf05da9e`, the same test reports the two expected later-worker-failure assertion failures; the success-preservation method passes. Restoring the exact PR production source restores a passing run.\n- Changed-file pre-commit and diff checks pass. [Full upstream lint](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35327695359) passes at `22fc9b9d9c6959e53200567856dd7f1aebb7de3b`, including all four Rust hooks. This covers the Rust workspace Clippy hook that could not run locally because Cargo reported `no VCS found for this package`.\n- Upstream CPU CI has not run: the prior head's test workflows were blocked by the missing `run-ci` label. No GPU profiler or HTTP end-to-end test was run.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis reports partial failure; it does not roll back profiling already started on successful workers. It changes neither model outputs nor the inference execution path, so model accuracy and throughput benchmarks are not applicable.\n\nRelated #39506 handles snapshot exceptions inside the scheduler profiler; this change handles aggregation of worker responses at the tokenizer and does not modify those files.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35327695923](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35327695923)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35327695698](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35327695698)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35327695903](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35327695903)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
